rs  to the end he maintained he was the  victim of an opposition plot  following his own efforts to introduce  anti-corruption reforms  live now to mariana sanchez in lima  viscara came out to speak in the last  hour what was his reaction  that's right imran martin viscara was  flanked by members of his cabinet in  front of the steps of the presidential  palace he gave a last goodbye to  peruvians he  has said goodbye he said he was going  home  but that he disagreed with the result of  this vote  and that he has always been transparent  he said he would not take any legal  action  and that he was now going to face  justice and prove  everyone wrong he has said all along not  only today but throughout these past  months  this during this impeachment and during  the past impeachment uh proceedings  a month and a half ago that he has  uh denied throughout this time  any wrongdoings and that well  and that he will prove everyone wrong in  the meantime  a lot of peruvians are now angry  in uh the last few polls uh we have seen  that  peruvian supported president martin  viscara and now people are protesting  the streets of  lima some also in the city of trujillo  north of  lima and in other places with just in  few people there is a curfew here in an  hour  because of the pandemic so possibly we  will see more people on the streets  tomorrow  i remind you that it's uh 80  78 of peruvians who have supported  viscara all along and have said that he  should stay that he should have stayed  until  july of next year we have elections  general elections  in jan in april and that he should stay  and face justice after that people are  angry  95 percent of peruvian say that he must  be  uh investigated and prosecuted but  uh but at this moment a lot of peruvians  are angry  and possibly will see more people in the  streets in the next few hours  thank you mariano sanchez life for us  there in peru
 

